      "content": "okay i get it, you have to be careful. but i'm just looking for the logic so i can make an informed choice. i read online that seroquel and xanax are both just sedatives, so wouldn't they basically just do the same thing? like, if i just take like a quarter of a pill, is there really any risk of something actually life-threatening happening, or is it just gonna make me extra sleepy? i'm just trying to figure out if this is a \"call the doctor immediately\" situation or just a \"maybe don't do it\" situation.",
